course: dictionary
lesson: 3439
title: Eyespots: false eyes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eyespot is a round patch of colour that looks like an eye. Butterflies, moths and some fish have them, and they can scare or fool predators, which are the animals that hunt them. «Big eyespots on a moth's wings can startle a bird», because the bird thinks something large and watchful is looking back.
explain: Eyespots near the wing tips work in a clever way. «Small eyespots near the wing tips draw pecks away from the head», so the bird attacks the false eye instead of the real head. That is why «butterflies with a torn eyespot often survive»: the attack landed on the fake eye.
explain: In science, the word means something much smaller. An eyespot is a tiny light-sensitive spot on very simple living things, such as Euglena, and it helps them find light. The same word is used for a patch on a wing and a spot on a single cell, so read the context to see which one it means.
fact: An eyespot is a round patch of colour that looks like an eye.
fact: «Eyespot» means a patch that looks like an eye, used to scare or fool predators.
fact: Eyespots can be found on butterfly and moth wings, and on the bodies of some fish.
fact: In science, an eyespot is a tiny light-sensitive spot that helps very simple living things find light.
fact: A predator is an animal that hunts other animals for food.
exercise: «Big eyespots on a moth's wings can startle a bird.» What can big eyespots do to a bird? | Hide it from light | *Startle it | Feed it | Make it sing
exercise: «Small eyespots near the wing tips draw pecks away from the head.» Where do the pecks go? | To the head | *To the false eye on the wing | To the tail | To the ground
exercise: In science, what does an eyespot on Euglena help it do? | *Find light | Hide underground | Fly over the water | Grow a hard shell
test: Which of these animals can have eyespots? | *A butterfly | A pencil | A rock | A cloud
test: What is a predator? | *An animal that hunts other animals | A bright patch of colour on a fish | A kind of camouflage | A plant that grows in water
exam: What is the main job of an eyespot on a butterfly's wing? | *To scare or fool predators | To help the butterfly sleep | To make the wing heavier | To carry food to the body
